WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.610
Before Infinity War, real and permanent death
among heroes was rare in the MCU, but now

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:10.710
as we stare down Endgame, it seems to be more
of a possibility than ever before, and many

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:13.740
of our favorite characters might not escape
it this time.

00:00:14.020 --> 00:00:16.060
So it's time to talk odds.

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:20.920
If you really wanted to predict possible outcomes
like Doctor Strange meditating over the Time

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:26.210
Stone, you could say that Carol Danvers, played
by Brie Larson, can absolutely die in just

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:27.200
her second film.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:31.539
You could argue that she's the best candidate
to go toe to toe with Thanos while the other

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:35.080
surviving Avengers are working on their secret
plan to undo the snap.

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.920
Being in the line of fire would place her
in clear mortal danger.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:43.940
And it could be poetic that Carol, who only
just arrived back on Earth, would sacrifice

00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:46.260
herself like the space god she is.

00:00:46.629 --> 00:00:50.660
You could even argue that, since there are
more than two decades separating Endgame and

00:00:50.660 --> 00:00:53.940
Captain Marvel, Carol wouldn't really even
be "dead."

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:57.740
Marvel could keep churning out movies set
in the intervening years.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:58.820
You'd be wrong.

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:03.800
Carol is the vanguard leading the charge into
a new age of the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.280
She'll stick around, and her chance of survival
is very high.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:12.620
Everyone's favorite raccoon with Bradley Cooper's
voice is already in a pretty bad spot when

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:13.980
Endgame begins.

00:01:14.080 --> 00:01:16.880
He's on an unfamiliar planet, far from home.

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:21.500
As far as he knows, he's the only surviving
member of the Guardians of the Galaxy, and,

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:26.320
most importantly, he watched his best friend
Groot crumble to dust before his eyes.

00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:31.170
Rocket and Thor had a conversation in Infinity
War about how hard you fight when it seems

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:32.620
you've got nothing left to lose.

00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:34.460
"I could lose a lot.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:36.520
Me, personally, I could lose a lot."

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.760
For Rocket, that time has arrived.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:44.180
Rocket and Groot have become sort of unofficial
mascots for the comic side of the MCU.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:48.640
With a third Guardians movie on the way, it's
hard to imagine a world in which they don't

00:01:48.649 --> 00:01:53.039
both pull through this, even if Rocket does
end up having to wear one of those prosthetics

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.500
he finds so hilarious.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:55.860
His chance of survival?

00:01:56.020 --> 00:01:57.020
Moderately high.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:01.939
Endgame's marketing materials have been very
clear about what the surviving heroes' goal

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:03.620
is: "Take it all back…"

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:05.039
"Whatever it takes."

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:09.319
That's a pretty clear mission statement that
gives every major character a redemptive arc

00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:11.580
as they each quest for personal vengeance.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:15.460
Bruce Banner, played by Mark Ruffalo, in particular
has a goal.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:20.720
Endgame will have to address Banner's sudden
inability to handle the Hulk, who has retreated

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.480
into his host body and refused to fight on
behalf of Banner and his friends.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:28.880
This left our heroes at an apparent disadvantage
during the Battle of Wakanda.

00:02:29.420 --> 00:02:33.040
While Banner overcame it, he and the Hulk
still have to have a conversation that will

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:34.120
resolve in Endgame.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:39.080
That resolution could ultimately end with
the Hulk choked out by Thanos' tremendous

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.500
power, but that seems unlikely.

00:02:41.760 --> 00:02:46.380
Possible remaining romantic tension with Black
Widow just gives him too much to do in the

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:47.500
MCU besides dying.

00:02:47.880 --> 00:02:49.560
His chance of survival is moderate.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:55.299
Some may argue that Black Widow, played by
Scarlett Johansson, can't possibly die in

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:57.940
Avengers: Endgame because she has a movie
in development.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:02.420
But it's also true that her film could be
a prequel about her early years as a spy,

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:05.000
which would make her current status a moot
point.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:09.760
There's honestly a strong case for killing
Natasha, and it all goes back to the very

00:03:09.760 --> 00:03:11.120
first Avengers film.

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:13.680
"I got red in my ledger.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.560
I'd like to wipe it out."

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:20.100
She's a character who's always had tension
bubbling beneath her cool exterior, which

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:24.820
suggests she will never be sated unless can
die heroically to wipe away that red.

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:29.120
That said, there are other characters whose
deaths would probably be more compelling to

00:03:29.129 --> 00:03:34.440
the overall story, and it's very easy to see
Natasha's being pretty useful in the MCU going

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:34.940
forward.

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:39.260
There's a world in which she could become
the new generation's Nick Fury, an advisor

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:43.560
and spymaster who's seen it all, done it all,
and has a cool head under pressure.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:45.560
Her chance of survival is moderate.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:50.020
Paul Rudd's Ant-Man clearly has a big role
to play in Endgame.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:54.379
In his previous films, two solo adventures
and a supporting role in Captain America:

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:57.220
Civil War, he's primarily played a comedic
role.

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:01.700
He sat out Infinity War, but his journey to
the Quantum Realm at the end of Ant-Man and

00:04:01.701 --> 00:04:06.230
the Wasp suggests he might have some scientific
answers for how the team can change history

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:07.360
and defeat Thanos.

00:04:07.740 --> 00:04:11.440
He's front-and-center this time around, which
means a greater risk of death.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:17.220
The Wasp could very easily be resurrected
and take his place in a future Avengers lineup,

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:21.520
and his daughter Cassie, a Marvel Comics superhero
in her own right, could take over.

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:26.300
But Scott Lang still seems to have more heroic
potential left in him, so let's hope he gets

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:29.780
to keep having his little, or sometimes giant,
adventures.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:31.480
He has a moderate chance of survival.

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:36.740
In the lead-up to Avengers: Infinity War and
Avengers: Endgame, two major character deaths

00:04:36.740 --> 00:04:38.600
have been discussed more than any other.

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:42.760
One we'll get to later, but the other is Robert
Downey Jr.'s Iron Man.

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:48.540
Tony Stark is the godfather of the MCU, the
original hero who launched it all.

00:04:48.540 --> 00:04:49.720
Sometimes he's saved the world.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.260
Sometimes he caused the problems.

00:04:51.670 --> 00:04:55.320
But he's always been there, and his journey
has all been building to this confrontation

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:56.140
with Thanos.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:05:01.240
What better way for it to end than for Tony
and the Mad Titan to go down at the same time?

00:05:01.240 --> 00:05:05.180
It would be a poetic ending, but is it really
what's in store for Tony Stark?

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:10.000
If any of the MCU's major characters could
have a life beyond superheroics, funding and

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:14.690
supporting and cheering on future Avengers
as a benefactor, it's him, so his chance of

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:16.180
survival is questionable.

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:21.160
The journey of Chris Hemsworth's Thor as a
fallen hero with nothing left to lose, pushing

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:25.100
for one last shot at victory makes up the
backbone of Infinity War.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:30.120
His story runs from the very first scene all
the way to the seconds before the snap, when

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:32.620
he embeds Stormbreaker in Thanos' chest.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:37.580
Heading into Endgame, all the Avengers bear
a burden of loss and defeat, but Thor bears

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:38.780
it more than the others.

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:43.560
It's easy to see how Thor could be marching
to his own death in Endgame, and how his final

00:05:43.560 --> 00:05:46.360
act of redemption could be one of self-sacrifice.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:52.040
Chris Hemsworth has been in the MCU since
2011, so his retirement could be imminent.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:57.200
But simply sending Thor off to try and rebuild
Asgard, having restored himself as a hero,

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.060
could be just as satisfying.

00:05:59.060 --> 00:06:01.360
So his chance of survival is questionable.

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:07.000
James "Rhodey" Rhodes, a.k.a. War Machine,
is one of the MCU's original superheroes.

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:11.560
He was introduced in its very first film,
played by Terrence Howard, gained a superhero

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:16.510
identity in Iron Man 2, in which Don Cheadle
took on the role, and has been a player many

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:18.100
major stories since.

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:22.000
The running joke has always sort of been that
Rhodey isn't quite as relevant and powerful

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.960
as Iron Man, which is noted in Avengers: Age
of Ultron.

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:26.760
"Why do I even talk to you guys?

00:06:26.770 --> 00:06:28.040
Everywhere else that story kills."

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:29.360
"That's the whole story?"

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:30.840
"Yes, the War Machine story."

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:32.840
"It's very good then."

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:37.870
His primary role in Captain America: Civil
War was as a casualty, and in Infinity War

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:40.640
he never rose above supporting character status.

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:45.480
War Machine seems primed for an Endgame appearance
that could elevate him by ending his story

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:47.080
with a blaze of glory.

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:51.460
Watching Rhodey go down fighting could be
a satisfying way to bid farewell to a character

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:55.590
who's been around for more than a decade,
and it could give Tony Stark the drive to

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:57.520
keep funding the Avengers in his honor.

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:01.700
For those reasons, we're putting his chance
of survival at moderately low.

00:07:02.460 --> 00:07:07.020
Hawkeye was conspicuously absent from Infinity
War, but his emotional journey is going to

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:08.620
be a major part of Endgame.

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:13.440
Avengers: Age of Ultron told us that when
he's not out saving the world, Clint Barton,

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:16.440
played by Jeremy Renner, has a family he loves
dearly.

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:20.510
And the second Endgame trailer revealed a
mentor relationship with a young girl who

00:07:20.510 --> 00:07:21.920
could be a future Hawkeye.

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:25.120
By Endgame, Clint has apparently lost all
that.

00:07:25.620 --> 00:07:29.310
He's a vigilante, taking on what's left of
the world through violence before his old

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:31.300
friend Natasha comes to retrieve him.

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:34.040
That sets up two potential outcomes.

00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:38.600
Either he does his part as a member of a successful
mission and reunites with his resurrected

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:41.700
family, or he dies trying to give them their
lives back.

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:47.060
Both are very possible, but watching a broken
Clint Barton make the final sacrifice on behalf

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:52.200
of his children seems like an emotional power
play the filmmakers might not be able to resist.

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:54.800
His chance of survival is moderately low.

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:58.740
In the comic The Infinity Gauntlet, Nebula
is a key character.

00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:01.980
She actually ends up wielding the Infinity
Gauntlet herself.

00:08:02.480 --> 00:08:06.320
We're not predicting anything like that for
Karen Gillan's film version of Nebula, but

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:08.400
she could have an important role in Endgame.

00:08:08.850 --> 00:08:13.260
Nebula comes into the film as the one remaining
character who knows Thanos intimately, and

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:17.260
she's also well aware of what he did to her
sister Gamora in Infinity War.

00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:21.940
Since Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 2 Nebula
has been on a redemptive arc that led to her

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:24.640
fighting alongside the Avengers and the Guardians.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:29.200
Now, with a possible way to defeat Thanos
in sight, she's not likely to slow down.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:33.860
Endgame presents a very clear opportunity
for Nebula to sacrifice herself.

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:38.500
It's hard to see her walking away alive, so
her chance of survival is low.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:42.180
Steve Rogers has been knocked down yet again
by a bully.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:45.010
He's sure to stand up with his fists raised
and declare,

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:46.520
"I could do this all day."

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:52.139
Captain America, played by Chris Evans, turned
out to have a limited role in Avengers: Infinity

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:56.760
War, but the snap has left him as the de facto
leader of the remaining Avengers on Earth.

00:08:56.940 --> 00:09:00.800
Trailers are placing him in a key position
as the man who will lead the fight to take

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:01.820
back the universe.

00:09:02.470 --> 00:09:06.180
Repeated hints that Evans is done with the
role after eight years suggest that Captain

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:08.180
America is going to die.

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:12.640
We can't know for sure, even if it is true
that Evans is walking away from the role after

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:13.140
Endgame.

00:09:13.340 --> 00:09:18.900
Captain America could simply quietly retire
to a cabin somewhere, content to split logs.

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:21.100
He could step away from active Avengers duty.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:25.480
But none of that would be very climactic,
so he could very well go down fighting, leaving

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:29.900
a grateful universe to mourn him while Tony
Stark continues to protect Earth.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:34.300
It's impossible to know for sure, but the
death of the First Avenger certainly seems

00:09:34.300 --> 00:09:35.200
to be approaching.

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:37.640
His chance of survival is very low.

00:09:38.420 --> 00:09:42.600
Even as we talk about all these horrible character
deaths, Avengers: Endgame is a film in which

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:46.480
more major characters could end up resurrected
than permanently dead.

00:09:46.980 --> 00:09:50.870
For example, Black Panther and Spider-Man
have movies approaching so we shouldn't expect

00:09:50.870 --> 00:09:51.800
them to stay dead.

00:09:51.940 --> 00:09:57.140
Nor are Shuri, the Wasp, Bucky, Falcon, Scarlet
Witch, and Vision likely to stay down, since

00:09:57.180 --> 00:09:59.080
they all seem to have promising futures.

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:03.780
In a world in which the Avengers restore many
of their friends, what does death really mean?

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:07.940
It's a comic book world, so deaths are almost
never permanent in the long run.

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:09.560
Will that change here?

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:14.080
One thing that seems very clear about Endgame
is that it's bound to rewrite the rules of

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:14.880
the MCU.

